{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>וְצִוְּךָ</b> — twice in the Masorah: here, and the other: וְצִוְּךָ לְנָגִיד — meaning, if Elohim commands you in this matter you can be a leader, for in another matter you cannot stand." "<b>עַל מְקֹמוֹ</b> — twice in the Masorah: here, and the other: וְהִתְבּוֹנַנְתָּ עַל מְקֹמוֹ וְאֵינֶנּוּ — to teach: if you administer justice below, there is peace; and if not, they administer justice against him above. And this is: וְהִתְבּוֹנַנְתָּ עַל מְקֹמוֹ וְאֵינֶנּוּ."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:34.919374240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}